ss of gun. He also names background checks and safe storage, and nowhere calls for banning civilian ownership in general. I coded it as `statement-other` (his own words, not an answer to a question put to him), in-term and chair-shaped.\n- **Judgement call:** rung 2 also needs \"while allowing other firearms\", and the newsletter never says that outright. I counted it as met, following the annex: a ban on a named class sets the boundary and leaves other guns legal. A stricter reader could apply the \"silence is not a clause\" rule here and code BLANK `direction-only` instead. The evidence tier would be `single-source`.\n- **The HB 1296 (2022) vote:** I coded his Nay on the permitless-carry conference report (69–30) as a record across two passages: the roll call and the enrolled bill text. It only rules out rung 5, so it is `direction-only` and not in `rests_on`.\n- **Quotes:**\n  - The \"banning assault rifles\" sentence is tagged `lever` and quotable.\n  - \"I voted against that law…\" is tagged `none` and not quotable (`not-forward`), because it looks back at a past vote.\n- **Left out:** I didn't code two sources.\n  - The HB 1296 details page lists the authors and does not show any action by Pierce.\n  - The 2026 forum transcript has nothing on guns.\n- **`needs_source`:** empty.","ttft_ms":31384,"type":"result","duration_ms":54435,"uuid":"aec8346a-0d98-4e82-b672-457771a3eaae","ttft_stream_ms":2008,"time_to_request_ms":122,"first_content_frame_ms":2009,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
